.TH VCAM 1 "2026-10-19" "vcam 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vcam \- control the vcam virtual camera
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vcam
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR PATH ]
.IR COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vcam
is the command line client for
.BR vcamd (1).
It connects to the daemon over a Unix socket and sends a single request per
invocation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-socket PATH
Path to the daemon control socket. Defaults to
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/vcam.sock .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start [\-\-source FILE] [\-\-no\-loop]
Start playing a video. Uses the configured source when
.B \-\-source
is omitted.
.TP
.B stop
Stop playback and show the black placeholder.
.TP
.B pause
Pause playback, keeping the last frame on screen.
.TP
.B resume
Resume playback.
.TP
.B seek POSITION
Seek to a position given as
.IR SS ,
.IR MM:SS " or " HH:MM:SS .
.TP
.B source FILE [\-\-no\-loop]
Change the source video without restarting the daemon.
.TP
.B loop on|off
Turn looping on or off for the current source.
.TP
.B output [\-\-width N] [\-\-height N] [\-\-fps N] [\-\-pixel\-format NV12|YUYV] [\-\-fit letterbox|fill|stretch] [\-\-mirror true|false] [\-\-rotate 0|90|180|270] [\-\-force]
Change the virtual camera output format. A change that renegotiates the device
caps is deferred while applications are using the camera, unless
.B \-\-force
is given.
.TP
.B consumers
List the applications currently holding the camera open.
.TP
.B profile list
List the configured
.B [[profiles]]
and which one is active.
.TP
.B profile use NAME [\-\-force]
Apply the named profile and pin it (turns automatic selection off).
.TP
.B profile auto on|off
Turn automatic profile selection on or off. Turning it on re-resolves the
output immediately.
.TP
.B compat on|off
Turn the Chromium/Electron compatibility shim on or off. When it is on (the
default) the daemon advertises
.B YUYV
while a Chromium-based application such as Discord, Chrome or Slack is
running, because those applications routinely fail to list a loopback device
that only offers
.BR NV12 .
The configured pixel format is restored when they exit.
.TP
.B status [\-\-json]
Print daemon status.
.TP
.B doctor [\-\-device PATH]
Run diagnostics on the module, device, access permissions and GStreamer
elements, and report the Chromium/Electron compatibility state. This runs
locally and does not require a running daemon. Use
.B \-\-device
to check a device other than the configured one.
.TP
.B reload
Reload the configuration file.
.TP
.B shutdown
Ask the daemon to exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Used to locate the default control socket.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Used to locate the default configuration file
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/vcam/config.toml .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vcamd (1),
.BR vcam-gui (1)
